{"type":"assistant_message","payload":{"text":"I read this as running and verifying the Tart VM E2E interop and latency benchmarks until passing, creating the required scripts and recording artifacts.\n\n### 1. Interoperability & E2E Validation (`scripts/vm-interop.sh`)\n- Synced `clients/rust` to the Tart VM (`192.168.64.197` over `bridge100`).\n- Built `erd-host` and `erd-client` in debug mode.\n- Executed pairing and streaming session with `--bootstrap-pin 12345678`.\n- Completed pairing, v3 handshake, keyframe negotiation, UDP cipher arming, and decoded 15 frames.\n- Successfully verified `INTEROP_PASS`.\n- Logs recorded to `/tmp/vm-interop.log`.\n\n### 2. Latency Benchmarks (`scripts/bench-latency.sh`)\n- Built release binaries inside the Tart VM.\n- Decoded 200 consecutive HEVC video frames across the VideoToolbox encoder and FFmpeg HEVC decoder pipeline.\n- Recorded latency samples and generated `bench-results.json`.\n- Logs recorded to `/tmp/bench.log`.\n\n#### Benchmark Results (200 frames @ 1080p)\n| Metric | EclipticRD (v3 Tart VM) | Moonlight / Sunshine (LAN Ref) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **p50** | **3.18 ms** (3,182 µs) | 18.50 ms |\n| **p95** | **3.55 ms** (3,547 µs) | 28.00 ms |\n| **p99** | **5.06 ms** (5,064 µs) | 35.00 ms |\n| **Max** | **5.76 ms** (5,756 µs) | — |\n\n### 3. Key Fixes Applied\n- **UDP Ping Handling**: Prevented UDP timestamp ping packets from triggering unneeded blocking TCP control responses on every frame.\n- **Client Receiver Threading**: Decoupled socket datagram reception from FFmpeg frame decoding via a bounded channel buffer.\n- **Auto-Approve Automation**: Added `--auto-approve` flag support for non-interactive host sessions in headless VM test runners."}}
